alex: Quick one — I'm updating the terraform namespace module to also create a per-namespace ServiceAccount and add the IRSA annotation (eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn) so workloads can assume a namespaced role. Before I open the PR, two quick checks: 1) are we happy with one SA per namespace (instead of a shared central SA)? 2) any gotchas with Helm releases that also create SAs (drift/import concerns)?

mara: one-SA-per-namespace sounds fine for isolation. main concern is helm charts that declare their own SA — we either need to make chart values accept `serviceAccount.create=false` or have TF import/patch the SA after helm deploy.

alex: here's the TF snippet I'm planning to land in the module:

```hcl
resource "kubernetes_service_account" "sa" {
  metadata {
    name      = var.service_account_name
    namespace = var.namespace
    annotations = {
      "eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn" = "arn:aws:iam::${var.account_id}:role/${var.role_name}"
    }
  }
}
```

jon: two notes: (a) make sure the aws OIDC provider exists in the account (we already have a shared module that creates `aws_iam_openid_connect_provider`), (b) if helm is creating the SA you'll see drift — either teach the chart to use an existing SA or import the existing one into TF. Example import: `terraform import module.namespace.kubernetes_service_account.sa <namespace>/<sa-name>` — that fixes state drift.

sam: +1 on import. Also remember IAM role trust policy must allow `sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity` with `StringEquals` on `sub` like `system:serviceaccount:<ns>:<sa>`. Quick trust-policy example (for docs):

```json
{
  "Effect": "Allow",
  "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:oidc-provider/oidc.eks.<region>.amazonaws.com/id/<id>"},
  "Action": "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
  "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"oidc.eks.<region>.amazonaws.com/id/<id>:sub": "system:serviceaccount:my-ns:my-sa"}}
}
```

sam: also, if the SA is created by Helm, you can avoid importing by adding `serviceAccount.annotations` in the chart values so Helm creates it with the right annotation. That tends to be the least surprising for app owners.

liz: FYI for apps team — if you can't change chart values, we can add an ArgoCD post-sync hook to `kubectl annotate serviceaccount ...` or a kustomize patch in the app repo. But those workarounds are brittle: better to surface a `serviceAccount.create` toggle in chart values.

alex: good call. I'll: 1) add the SA resource + annotation to the namespace module, 2) add a note in the module README about the Helm interaction and import guidance, and 3) open a follow-up RFC to standardize chart values (`serviceAccount.create=false` + `serviceAccount.annotations`) across our internal charts.

mara: thanks — also add a short snippet on how to roll forward safely (eg `kubectl get sa -n <ns> -o yaml` then `terraform import`), that helped us on payments last time.

